xt"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window instead of inside it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Such players expose their own picture-in-picture facility with the missing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"piece — THEOplayer retains the window across source changes when the host","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constructs it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"PiPConfiguration(retainPresentationModeOnSourceChange: true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — but only if the window is driven through THAT facility. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol is how an adapter hands the SDK that steering wheel; the renderer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prefers it over its own controller whenever the content adapter conforms.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three members are called on the main thread (the renderer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":"); the change handler must likewise be invoked on the main"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thread, for every transition — including viewer-driven ones (the system UI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can dismiss the window at any time), which is the whole reason the handler"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exists: the break format follows what is actually on screen."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore/documentation/OptiViewAdsCore/PictureInPictureCapable/onPictureInPictureChange(_:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"onPictureInPictureChange","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"((","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4V